<BaseLayout title="Dynamic Stiffness and Disturbance Rejection — ECE/ME 732">
  <p class="crumb"><a href={href("/interactives/")}>← Interactives</a></p>
  <h1>Dynamic Stiffness and Disturbance Rejection</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    How well a regulated current source shrugs off a disturbance is one number
    per frequency: the disturbance it takes to move the output by one unit.
    That is a frequency response function with physical units, so it is plotted
    log-log rather than in dB. Resistance and inductance bought in hardware and
    the same gains bought in a controller land in the same place in the
    equation — and lift the same part of the curve.
  </p>
  <Widget />
</BaseLayout>
